{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-3-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-3-1","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.md","line":236,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.tex#def:dc-ch5-3-1","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.tex","label":"def:dc-ch5-3-1","line":521,"source":"\\begin{definition}[conjugate point, multiplicity]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch5-3-1}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch5-2-1}\n\n  \\dcref{ch5:3.1}\n  Let $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$ be a geodesic and $t_0\\in(0,a]$. The point\n  $\\gamma(t_0)$ is \\emph{conjugate} to $\\gamma(0)$ along $\\gamma$ if some\n  nonzero Jacobi field $J$ satisfies $J(0)=J(t_0)=0$. Its \\emph{multiplicity}\n  is the dimension of the space of such fields. Conjugacy along a geodesic\n  segment is symmetric under reversal of the segment.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[conjugate point, multiplicity] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368352d332d31\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23def%3Adc-ch5-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch5-2-1</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:3.1</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$</span> be a geodesic and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_0\\in (0,a]$\">$t_0\\in (0,a]$</span>. The point <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t_0)$\">$\\gamma (t_0)$</span> is <em>conjugate</em> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (0)$\">$\\gamma (0)$</span> along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> if some nonzero Jacobi field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J$\">$J$</span> satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(0)=J(t_0)=0$\">$J(0)=J(t_0)=0$</span>. Its <em>multiplicity</em> is the dimension of the space of such fields. Conjugacy along a geodesic segment is symmetric under reversal of the segment. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#rem:dc-ch5-2-11","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#rem:dc-ch5-3-2","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch5-2-1"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#ex:dc-ch5-3-3","title":"ex:dc-ch5-3-3","label":"ex:dc-ch5-3-3"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-3-4","title":"def:dc-ch5-3-4","label":"def:dc-ch5-3-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#prop:dc-ch5-3-5","title":"prop:dc-ch5-3-5","label":"prop:dc-ch5-3-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#prop:dc-ch5-3-9","title":"prop:dc-ch5-3-9","label":"prop:dc-ch5-3-9"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#cor:dc-ch5-3-10","title":"cor:dc-ch5-3-10","label":"cor:dc-ch5-3-10"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-2","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-2","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate","titl